From: cerXXXX <polyakovia2009@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 10:39:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] feat: --stream renders without a window and streams the
 frames live

With --stream <url> (and --window for the size) the GLFW window is created
at the stream's size and never shown; every frame is read back and piped
to an ffmpeg child that encodes it with VA-API H.264 into MPEG-TS at the
given URL (e.g. udp://127.0.0.1:41234), timestamps from the wall clock and
SPS/PPS on every keyframe so players can join at any time. Meant for
showing a live scene where the engine's own surface can't be seen, like a
lock screen.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JnSVvFGk6GTNXvPXqCPwwh
